There is a box on my desk.
I open the box.
There are sweets inside the box.
My father looks at the screen.
He asks, "Maya, what is in the box?"
I smile.
I bring the box near the camera.
"Father, please look," I say.
"This is an Indian sweet."
"Its name is laddu."
My father asks, "Is your sweet good?"
"Yes, it is very tasty," I reply.
"This is my new favorite thing."
I take one laddu in my hand.
"I want to give this to you," I say.
"But you are in Mexico."
My father laughs.
"Yes, we are very far," he says.
"But your new city is very nice."
